  "privacyAccountsTitle": "Accounts and Credentials",
  "privacyAccountsBody": "Navis connects directly to the Subsonic or OpenSubsonic servers you configure. Server addresses and usernames are stored in the app database. Your server password and ListenBrainz token are stored in the platform's secure credential store when available. A Last.fm API key you enter yourself is stored in the app database.",
  "privacyScrobblingTitle": "External Scrobbling",
  "privacyScrobblingBody": "With a validated ListenBrainz token, Navis sends listening activity for played tracks to ListenBrainz while Scrobbling is on. This can include track title, artist, album, duration, play time and now-playing status. While Likes is on, songs you like are sent as loved. Your ListenBrainz token stays on your device.",
  "privacyDownloadsTitle": "Downloads and Cache",
  "privacyDownloadsBody": "Offline downloads, playback cache, artwork, lyrics, and library metadata are stored on your device so playback and browsing can work without repeatedly fetching the same data. You can clear cache data from Settings.",
  "privacyDiagnosticsTitle": "Diagnostics",
  "privacyDiagnosticsBody": "Navis avoids logging raw credentials and redacts sensitive authentication values from diagnostics. Network errors may still include service names or non-secret request context needed to troubleshoot failures. Startup details stay on this device until you copy them.",
  "privacySummary": "Navis does not operate a central account service for your music library. Data is exchanged with your servers and with the online services you leave on in Settings › Integrations.",
  "privacyReadFullPolicy": "Read the Full Privacy Policy",
  "@privacyReadFullPolicy": {
    "description": "Link at the end of the in-app Privacy page that opens the full policy on the Navis website."
  },
